{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And she spoke to him, etc., לֵאמֹר.</b> The meaning of his saying <b>לֵאמֹר</b> is that the men of the household would thus say testimony to the matter, and therefore you will find that his anger was not kindled against Joseph but only over the fact that she gave strength to her words by making it known to others. This is what it means by <b>when his master heard</b> etc. <b>לֵאמֹר, according to these things</b> etc. — for Scripture had no need to say anything other than ״when his master heard his wife's words,״ but rather it intended to say that his anger was kindled only when he heard that there were informants about the matter, which is what it says: ״לֵאמֹר, according to these things״ etc. It will be further explained nearby:" "<b>לֵאמֹר, according to these things, etc.</b> Meaning: not that he believed her, that things were indeed as her words [stated], but rather because his wife said so, a slight stir was made. And therefore he did not discipline him, nor do to him anything according to the standard punishment done to a slave who sets his eyes upon his master's wife."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:47:07.452906281Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}